{
  "work_package_id": "WP-004",
  "work_package_file": "work/WP-004.md",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "assigned_to": "QA",
  "dependencies": [
    "WP-003"
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "The orchestrator runs section updates without visible flicker — no full-page flash during data-only polls",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Scroll position in the orchestrator runs section is preserved across poll updates that don't change the runs list structure",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The status card (Running badge, elapsed time, PID, progress) updates in-place without rebuilding the entire runs list",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "When a new run appears or the active run becomes inactive, the runs list performs a structural re-render but saves and restores scroll position",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Log preview widgets continue to function correctly — they are NOT destroyed/recreated during data-only status card updates",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The kill button, dismiss button, and all existing run-event handlers continue to work after in-place status card updates",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "All unit tests in project-detail-scroll.test.ts pass",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-09T17:34:04Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-09T17:42:45Z",
      "duration_ms": 521000,
      "summary": [
        "Implemented flicker-free DOM patching and scroll preservation for the orchestrator runs section.",
        "Added _orchRunsStructureKey() pure helper: computes a stable JSON key from (sorted run filenames, activeFilename). Same key = same list structure = in-place patch is safe.",
        "Added _patchOrchStatusCard() helper: replaces innerHTML of #orch-status-card-container without touching sibling log preview widget. No-op when HTML unchanged.",
        "Modified renderRunsList(): (a) walks up to the nearest scrollable ancestor of #orchestrator-runs-section and saves scrollTop before innerHTML rebuild; (b) restores scrollTop after rebuild; (c) wraps the status card HTML in <div id=\"orch-status-card-container\"> for targeted patching.",
        "Modified pollQueue(): removed the top-of-function _pdLogPreviewCleanups drain (it was pre-empting the in-place path). Initialised lastRunsStructureKey=null so the first tick always falls through to a full renderRunsList. Subsequent ticks with the same structure key call _patchOrchStatusCard only — log preview widgets are not drained. Ticks with a different key (run left queue, new run appeared) fall through to a full renderRunsList with scroll preservation.",
        "Updated DOM contract comment in file header to document #orch-status-card-container.",
        "Created tests/gui/project-detail-scroll.test.ts with 19 unit tests covering: _orchRunsStructureKey (5 tests), _patchOrchStatusCard (4 tests), renderRunsList scroll/container ID (3 tests), pollQueue in-place vs structural (3 tests), log preview lifecycle (2 tests), event handler survival (2 tests).",
        "All 3183 tests pass (105 test files) with no regressions."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/gui/public/views/project-detail.js",
          "mcp-server/tests/gui/project-detail-scroll.test.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:42:45Z",
          "note": "renderRunsList is a deeply nested closure inside getRunLogs().then() that closes over `sorted`, `repo`, `slug`, `activeFilename`, and now `lastRunsStructureKey`. The existing refactor-candidate comment (line ~1239) is accurate — extracting this as a module-level helper accepting (sorted, repo, slug, activeFilename, matchingQueueEntry, structureKeyRef) would improve testability. The WP-004 in-place patch changes make this slightly more complex to extract, but the opportunity remains valid for a future pass."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:42:45Z",
          "note": "The scroll-ancestor walk in renderRunsList (lines ~1268–1279) uses window.getComputedStyle to find a scrollable parent. In jsdom tests `window.getComputedStyle` returns empty objects so `overflowY` is always `''`, causing it to fall back to `document.documentElement`. This is correct behavior for tests but means the scroll-restore path is not exercised in jsdom for real scrollable elements. A future improvement could extract the scroll-anchor logic into a testable helper that accepts a custom getStyle function."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:42:45Z",
          "note": "pollQueue still calls renderOrchToolbar on every tick (both in-place and structural paths). renderOrchToolbar rebuilds the entire toolbar DOM including Kill and Resume buttons. A future pass could add a similar in-place patch for the toolbar's button enabled/disabled state when the queue entry hasn't structurally changed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-09T17:43:10Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-09T17:45:34Z",
      "duration_ms": 144000,
      "summary": [
        "All 19 unit tests in project-detail-scroll.test.ts pass. Full regression: 105 test files, 3183 tests — 0 failures.",
        "AC1 PASS: In-place path calls _patchOrchStatusCard() only — no full innerHTML rebuild of runsEl, no page flash.",
        "AC2 PASS: scrollTop saved before runsEl.innerHTML rebuild and restored immediately after; data-only path skips renderRunsList entirely so scroll is untouched.",
        "AC3 PASS: _patchOrchStatusCard targets only #orch-status-card-container, leaving the surrounding runs list DOM intact.",
        "AC4 PASS: When match becomes null (run left queue) the structure key differs from lastRunsStructureKey, triggering the structural else-branch with renderRunsList + scroll preserve.",
        "AC5 PASS: #orch-project-log-preview is a sibling of #orch-status-card-container (not a child), so _patchOrchStatusCard innerHTML replacement never touches it. Log preview cleanup only drained on structural rebuilds (confirmed by §5 tests).",
        "AC6 PASS: renderOrchToolbar executes on every poll tick (both paths), so Kill/dismiss/toolbar buttons are always current. §6 tests confirm buttons and View links survive in-place updates.",
        "AC7 PASS: 19/19 unit tests pass."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "19 new tests covering _orchRunsStructureKey (5), _patchOrchStatusCard (4), renderRunsList scroll/container (3), pollQueue branch (3), log preview lifecycle (2), event handler survival (2)",
        "tests_passed": 3183,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "code-smell",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:45:34Z",
          "note": "Double-drain of _pdLogPreviewCleanups in the structural rebuild path: both the caller (pollQueue structural branch, onKillDone, catch handler) and renderRunsList itself drain the array. The second drain is a no-op (array is already []) so this is benign, but the redundancy is confusing and could lead to issues if renderRunsList is ever called from a path that didn't pre-drain. Low risk given current call sites, but worth a cleanup pass."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:45:34Z",
          "note": "The scroll-ancestor walk in renderRunsList falls back to document.documentElement when no scrollable ancestor is found. In the jsdom test environment window.getComputedStyle returns empty objects so overflowY is always empty string, meaning the walk always falls back to documentElement. The scroll-restore path is exercised in tests via the data attribute workaround on orchContainer, but the IIFE walk itself is not exercised in jsdom. Consider extracting the walk into a testable helper with an injectable getStyle callback (noted by Developer; raised here for Reviewer awareness)."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:45:34Z",
          "note": "No observations blocking merge — code is correct and all acceptance criteria are met."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-06-09T17:34:04Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-06-09T17:45:34Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:42:45Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 7 acceptance criteria met. Full test suite passes (3183 tests, 0 failures).",
        "Key files changed: mcp-server/gui/public/views/project-detail.js (added _orchRunsStructureKey, _patchOrchStatusCard, modified renderRunsList and pollQueue), mcp-server/tests/gui/project-detail-scroll.test.ts (new — 19 unit tests).",
        "The in-place patch triggers when: same run filenames + same activeFilename (queue match still present). The structural rebuild triggers when: match is null (run left queue) or lastRunsStructureKey is null (first tick). Log preview cleanup is only drained on structural rebuilds, not on data-only status card updates.",
        "DOM contract: #orch-status-card-container wraps the status card HTML inside .orch-active-run-section. It is a sibling of #orch-project-log-preview (not a parent). The log preview widget survives in-place updates because only the container innerHTML is replaced."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:45:34Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 7 ACs verified green. 3183 tests pass, 0 regressions.",
        "One low-priority code-smell flagged: double-drain of _pdLogPreviewCleanups in structural rebuild paths (pollQueue, onKillDone, catch handler all drain before calling renderRunsList, which also drains internally). Benign no-op today but slightly confusing — worth a cleanup note in code review.",
        "scroll-ancestor walk is not exercised via jsdom's getComputedStyle (always returns empty overflowY); test §3.1 works around this via a data-attribute scrollTop stub. The walk itself is correct for browser use. Reviewer may want to note the extractable helper opportunity.",
        "No blocking issues. Implementation is ready for code review."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

